  "dcterms:publisher": "U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (CompTox Chemicals Dashboard / DSSTox)",
  "biobricks:reviewed": false,
  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by BioBricks licensing-annotation agent (Claude Opus). The brick pulls CPCat.zip from EPA's public gaftp server; the EPA CompTox Chemicals Dashboard chemistry content is distributed as public-domain U.S. Government data (data.gov catalog record), hence class=open / commercial=permitted. HUMAN CHECK REQUIRED: per the README, CPCat is a compilation that ingests third-party sources including the DrugBank database (which carries its own more-restrictive license for its native distribution) and the Nordic SPIN database. EPA releases the compiled CPCat product publicly as government data, but a reviewer should confirm no embedded DrugBank/SPIN content triggers separate upstream obligations. Confidence medium.",
